# One HTML escape for markup a Term task builds as text. Every value that did not come from the page's own literals
# goes through `escape-html` before it is joined into a body: `&` first, so an entity already written is not read
# twice, then `<`, `>`, `"` and `'`, which makes the result safe both as element text and inside a quoted attribute.
# It is the same set the node serializer's `escapeText` and `escapeAttr` apply (dom/native/node/runtime/html.ts),
# written in Term so it runs on every backend a site is cast to.

load @term/base/text
  find replace-all

task escape-html
  take value, like text
  like text
  save out
    call replace-all
      read value
      text <&>
      text <&amp;>
  save out
    call replace-all
      read out
      text <\<>
      text <&lt;>
  save out
    call replace-all
      read out
      text <\>>
      text <&gt;>
  save out
    call replace-all
      read out
      text <">
      text <&quot;>
  save out
    call replace-all
      read out
      text <'>
      text <&#39;>
  send back, read out
